# File: tests/features/add_greeting_unique_char_count_library_helper.feature
# Generated from: specs/237-add-greeting-unique-char-count-library-helper/requirements.md
Feature: Count distinct characters in the completed greeting

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Count distinct characters in the completed greeting
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_unique_char_count is called with Ada, Bob, and Ada Lovelace
    Then the results are the Python int values 9, 8, and 12

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Count is case-sensitive and per Unicode code point
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_unique_char_count is called with ADA and Zo plus U+00EB
    Then the results are 8 and 8

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Preserve invalid-name behavior
    Given the invalid names empty, space-tab, None, and 42
    When greeting_unique_char_count is called with each invalid name
    Then each call raises ValueError with message name must not be blank

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Expose and document the helper without changing the CLI
    Given the README Library section
    When the README Library example runs and prints greeting_unique_char_count of Ada
    Then it prints 9 and greeting_unique_char_count is listed in nmg_sdlc_smoke.__all__
    And the README documents code-point case-sensitive distinctness, completed-greeting scope, and inherited invalid-name error
    And nmg-smoke Ada still prints exactly Hello, Ada and exits with status 0
